<title>USA: Vinik group ups Consolidated Graphics stake.</title>
<headline>Vinik group ups Consolidated Graphics stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Boston investor Jeffrey Vinik said Thursday it raised its stake in Consolidated Graphics Inc to 1,181,700 common shares, or 9.5 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include the purchase of 201,400 common shares between February 20 and February 26 at prices ranging from $27.1980 to $30.9183 per share.</p>
<p>Consolidated Graphics is a Houston, Tx.,-based commercial printing company.</p>
